      "writtenOn": "2025-11-21T21:44:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder if this could be replaced with:\n\n1. `std::is_layout_compatible_v` (which IIUC also covers field offsets+types;  and AFAIK Skia started recently allowing usage of C++20 features)\n2. `std::is_standard_layout_v` (this is probably redundant wrt `std::is_layout_compatible_v`, but it seems that it wouldn\u0027t hurt covering this explicitly)\n3. `is_trivially_copyable_v`\n\n?\n\nThis review comment is mostly motivated by the desire to detect future scenarios where these structs change in `memcpy`-incompatible ways.  I guess these structs are unlikely to change, but it still seems desirable to document why `memcpy` is safe.\n\nFWIW this comment also applies to other `static_assert` / `sizeof(...)` / `memcpy` in this `.cc` file.\n\nPS. For longer-term I\u0027ve also opened https://crbug.com/462770920, but I guess that this won\u0027t help in the short-term... :-(",
