      "message": "Does that imply that the caller has to guarantee that the lifetime of `*out_skcms` will not be longer than the lifetime of `rust_profile`?  If so, then:\n\n* Can you please add this to the doc comment here?\n* Is it actually possible to fulfill this guarantee in `SkPngRustCodec.cpp`?  See for example the problem fixed by https://review.skia.org/917191.\n\n---------------------------------\n\nIf the 2nd item above is a concern, then I wonder if it may be possible for `FFI.rs` to propagate the `\u0027input` lifetime into the output.  Hand-waving:\n\n```\npub fn parse_icc_profile\u003c\u0027input\u003e(\n    data: \u0026\u0027input [u8],\n    out: \u0026mut ffi::IccProfile\u003c\u0027input\u003e,\n) -\u003e bool { ... }`?\n```\n\n(Maybe this can be done in a follow-up CL and for now we can just leave a TODO?)",
