      "writtenOn": "2025-11-21T21:44:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you please use the technique from https://cxx.rs/shared.html#extern-enums to make `cxx::bridge` generate code that ensures that enum values match on both sides of the FFI boundary?\n\nThis may require some additional changes - e.g. to provide a name for [the anonymous enum](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/modules/skcms/src/skcms_public.h;l\u003d325-357;drc\u003d410256218592fb34586325b4e065a0325256e868) defined in `skcms_public.h`.  And this may also require indicating that the enum comes from a different C/C++ namespace than the other types around - see https://cxx.rs/attributes.html?highlight\u003dnamespace#namespace\n\nI am also a bit confused why `YCbCR \u003d 4` above but `skcms_public.h` says `skcms_Signature_YCbCr  \u003d 0x59436272`",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 130,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "e01443450c27062bb53b228fc21dc2161572539c",
