      "writtenOn": "2025-11-24T20:32:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for pointing this, I thought I matched the values to skcms but seems I lost this change. It is a difference between Skcms and moxcms: Skcms uses the values of this enum to compare with the actual signature, so the byte values found in the file correspond to this string. Moxcms has different constants for validating the signatures corresponding to each type and it is using an incremental indexed enum instead.\n\nIn the case of skcms_Signature_YCbCr  \u003d 0x59436272, signature corresponds to \"YCbr\" ASCI, which moxcms converts to the indexed enum:\n\nhttps://github.com/awxkee/moxcms/blob/0d051071233a890247a9470d117df6c0d755456a/src/profile.rs#L309\n\nAfter the change, I validated that if enum values do not match we would get reported a build error like this:\n\nbazel-out/k8-fastbuild/bin/rust/icc/FFI.rs.cc:710:15: error: static assertion failed due to requirement \u0027static_cast\u003cunsigned int\u003e(skcms_Signature::skcms_Signature_15CLR) \u003d\u003d 1178815571\u0027: disagrees with the value in #[cxx::bridge]\n  710 | static_assert(static_cast\u003c::std::uint32_t\u003e(skcms_Signature::skcms_Signature_15CLR) \u003d\u003d 1178815571, \"disagrees with the value in #[cxx::bridge]\");\n      |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nbazel-out/k8-fastbuild/bin/rust/icc/FFI.rs.cc:710:84: note: expression evaluates to \u00271178815570 \u003d\u003d 1178815571\u0027\n  710 | static_assert(static_cast\u003c::std::uint32_t\u003e(skcms_Signature::skcms_Signature_15CLR) \u003d\u003d 1178815571, \"disagrees with the value in #[cxx::bridge]\");\n      |               ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^~~~~~~~~~~~~\n1 error generated.",
      "parentUuid": "126830d0_0f87aa9c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 130,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "e01443450c27062bb53b228fc21dc2161572539c",
